# Jason Review Feedback — 2026-07-09

Status: authoritative human review feedback for the next North Star planning iteration. This feedback adopts planning defaults; it is not final North Star lock approval.

## Decisions

1. Every recommendation in the 2026-07-09 Verdify Skills adversarial review is adopted as the new planning default.
2. Safety work should stay narrow, but package publication must use a trusted installer and atomic publication, including the accepted integrity and provenance controls.
3. Verdify Skills is primarily an internal capability. It may be open sourced or referenced later, but building an external community is not a current product goal.
4. Backward compatibility is not required. Deprecated capabilities should be removed so the platform and skills stay light and simple.
5. Verdify Skills, Agent Platform, Orbit, and Gravity are all active pilot projects. Success means integrating all four into one system. Verdify Skills is the agent and method layer that binds and orchestrates that integration.
6. Jason (`jvallery`) and James (`jrvallery`) may approve releases. James is the current npm publisher. This does not change the separately accepted Jason-only North Star lock authority.
7. The old Gravity instance is not the current project. The restarted Gravity repository is the current active, in-flight source of truth.
8. Gravity should expose a versioned, tenant-scoped, read-only API with an MCP adapter.
9. Orbit is both Jason's personal assistant and the engineering chief of staff. Its intended information scope includes email, calendars, enterprise documents, transcriptions, notes, conversations, meetings, and engineering context. GOG is already entering the pod environment, and OpenClaw or Hermes may provide parts of the management layer. This broad scope requires governed connector identities, least privilege, audit, privacy, retention, and human control rather than a blanket connector exclusion.
10. Delivery should move as soon as safely possible without an artificial deadline. The objective is a tightly integrated, self-building four-project platform that can drive its own forward progress and support customer consulting. Verified platform gaps belong in GitHub Issues in the owning repositories. The root planning agent is the outer loop that keeps all four projects aligned to the common vision.

## Planning implications

- Replace a single non-Gravity pilot with one integrated four-project pilot and project-specific proof points.
- Keep the North Star unlocked until separate explicit signoff.
- Plan an immediate safety-only package patch and remove deprecated surfaces without compatibility shims when the owning implementation issues execute.
- Treat Gravity readiness as the trust gate for cross-platform consumption and promotion of the current active project, not as evidence that a retired deployment is the current product.
- Treat Orbit connector breadth as product scope and make security, privacy, retention, identity, audit, and user-control architecture requirements.
- Optimize sequencing and parallelism for fastest safe convergence rather than a calendar deadline.

